  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AMECEA Peacebuilding and Advocacy Mission to Sudan and South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The AMECEA peacebuilding and advocacy mission seeks to inspire hope and strengthen the Church&#x2019;s role as an agent of peace in Sudan and South Sudan amid ongoing political tensions and community-level violence. Rooted in AMECEA&#x2019;s mission to promote unity, justice, and solidarity, the project responds to fragile contexts marked by social fragmentation, weakened systems, and loss of trust. 

Phase I (February&#x2013;April 2026) will focus on foundational capacity strengthening and community-level peacebuilding in Juba as a strategic hub. The mission will combine pastoral accompaniment, collaborative engagement with local Church leadership, and regional and global advocacy for sustainable peace. Subsequent phases will extend outreach to conflict-affected areas such as Upper Nile State, ensuring inclusive engagement and coordinated action for long-term reconciliation and stability.</narrative>
  </description>
